course: dictionary
lesson: 15765
title: Trustworthiness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trustworthiness is the quality of being trustworthy. A trustworthy person is honest, reliable and can be trusted to do what is right. «Maya always gives back the change she finds, so her friends know she has trustworthiness.»
explain: Trustworthiness can also describe information. It means how reliable and true a source is, such as a website, a book or a news report. «The article had no author and no date, so Sam questioned its trustworthiness.» Sam is judging whether the information can be believed.
explain: To judge trustworthiness, ask who wrote the information and why. Then check whether other sources agree. «Jack read the same story on three different sites, and all three gave the same facts.» When sources agree, that is a clue the information is trustworthy.
explain: Stories show trustworthiness through actions. «Priya promised to keep Ben's secret, and she kept it even when it was hard.» Her actions prove her trustworthiness, not just her words.
fact: Trustworthiness means being honest, reliable and able to be trusted to do what is right.
fact: «Trustworthiness» is an uncountable noun, so we do not add an s to make it plural.
fact: Trustworthiness of information means how reliable and true it is.
fact: In citizenship lessons, honesty, respect and trustworthiness are core values.
fact: To judge a website, check who wrote it and whether other sources agree with it.
exercise: «Her friends know she is honest and always does what is right.» What quality does this show? | Tiredness | *Trustworthiness | Shyness | Hunger
exercise: «The website had no author, no date and no other site that agreed with it.» What does this suggest about its trustworthiness? | *Low, because nobody can check it | It has nothing to do with trustworthiness | High, because it has no author | Perfect, because it has no date
exercise: What does trustworthiness of information mean? | How long it is | How quickly it was written | *How reliable and true it is | How many pictures it has
test: «Priya kept Ben's secret even when it was hard.» What does this show about Priya? | *Her trustworthiness | Her hunger | Her height | Her favourite colour
test: Which is the best way to judge the trustworthiness of a website? | Ask whether it has a picture of a cat | *Check who wrote it and whether other sources agree | Count how many colours it uses | Pick the first result you see
exam: Which sentence best shows trustworthiness? | Ella says she found nothing at all | Ella forgets where she put the wallet | *Ella gives back the wallet she found, with all the money still inside | Ella hides the wallet in her bag
